    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` feature on the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**What the code does:** on owner creation, it assigns `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 LAST3 being the upper-cased first three letters of the last name, and NNNN a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. hsqldb is the test DB and runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared in SQL.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps `customerCode` on `toOwnerDto`; added `@Mapping(target = \"customerCode\", ignore = true)` to `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` since it's a create-time server value.\n\n5. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 a step function that computes the code: `sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, mutating the `@Val Owner` in place.\n\n6. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step between `build` and `save` (under `transaction` governance), so the owner exists but is not yet counted when the sequence is computed. This ordering makes the second owner's sequence exactly one more than the first's, satisfying the global-sequence assertion.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` test and the full suite pass.",
